{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/629915-hellboy-as-a-hunter","id":629915,"title":"Hellboy As A Hunter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-17T07:43:32-07:00","id":629915,"title":"Hellboy As A Hunter","content":"I think it could be pretty awesome. The only problem might reconciling the disparate elements of the NWOD and Hellboy franchises. Here is a character sheet for Hellboy, using material from Mirrors, 2ed Hunter and Werewolf, as well as a guideline for converting Willpower points into pseudo Essence and vice-versa, for the purposes of Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The BPRD could be adapted into the NWOD as a department of Task Force VALKYRIE with significant ties to the Null Mysteriis and VASCU. Most of its Hunters and other employees are working with the latter two organizations, or have worked for them.<br /> <br /> Hellboy may have varying degrees of sympathy for the Loyalists Of Thule. Liz could be a member of VASCU, while Abe could have been discovered by the Null Mysteriis. Hellboy could be an unusual member of the Lucifuge. There is no rule saying that the progenitors and ancestors of the Lucifuge have to consist entirely of straightforward Biblical demons. Giving him Castigations should be analyzed on a case by case basis. Be careful with conflicting elements of the two settings, though. Crossover with Beast: The Primordial might work, as well.<br /> <br /> I gave him the &quot;Absorb Energy&quot; and &quot;New Face&quot; Dread Powers to represent his immunity to fire/extreme heat, and to make it easier for him to his job in the NWOD without drawing too much attention. You don't have to use those Dread Powers exactly as described in Mortal Remains and Hunter's Core Rule Book. You don't have to give him the &quot;Regenerate&quot; Dread Power if you think Quick Healer 5 is enough. When we factor in Risking Willpower, expending Practical Beats (Mortal Remains -- Page 161), using certain Relics, Virtue, Vice, rest, Conditions/Tilts and personal victories, Hellboy's got more than enough Willpower points to activate his Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Friendly/Determined<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Temperamental<br /> <br /> <b>Profession:</b> Occultist<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Demonic Heir &amp; Occult Investigator<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 3, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Folklore &amp; Mythology) 3, Computer 1, Crafts (Firearm Maintenance) 3, Investigation (Detective Work) 4, Medicine (Herbs &amp; Remedies) 3, Occult (Charms &amp; Curses) 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl (Right Hand Of Doom) 5, Drive 2, Firearms 1, Larceny 1, Stealth (Urban) 3, Survival 3, Weaponry (Swords) 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken (Cats) 3, Empathy 3, Expression (Humor) 2, Intimidation (Physical Threats) 4, Persuasion 2, Socialize 1, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skill Tricks:</b> Investigation: Pattern Expert, Occult: Myth Expert, Brawl: Knockout Punch, Survival: Concrete Jungle, Streetwise: Rumor Mill<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Virtuous, Area Of Expertise (Detective Work), Professional Training 5 (Occultist: Occult, Investigation, Academics), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Herbs &amp; Remedies, Charms &amp; Curses), Patient, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Crafts, Medicine, Occult), Holistic Awareness, Library 3 (Occult, Medicine), Language (Ancient &amp; Supernatural), Multilingual X (ST Fiat), Trained Observer 1, Eye For The Strange, Tolerance For Biology, Indomitable, Ambidextrous, Disarm, Danger Sense, Quick Healer 5*, Fast Reflexes 2, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Hardy 3, Heavy Weapons (Swords, Right Hand Of Doom) 5, Demolisher 3, Fame 1 (Hunters), Alternate Identity 3, Inspiring, Iron Will, Allies 3/Status 3 (BPRD), Contacts 1 + X (BPRD, Various Supernaturals), True Friend (Abe, Liz, Bruttenholm), Fixer, Resources 2, Striking Looks +2 (Imposing), Esoteric Armory 3, Relic (Right Hand Of Doom)<br /> <br /> *Quick Healer 5: Hellboy's injuries heal 4 times faster, as opposed to the 2 times faster of Quick Healer 4. If you use the standard healing times for injuries, Hellboy heals 1 bashing every 4 minutes, 1 lethal every 12 hours and 1 aggravated every 42 hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter Tactics:</b> ST Fiat.<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8 [Risking Willpower + 6 Dots From Potency]<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Health:</b> 12 (Size 6)<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 8<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Armored Hide 3, Absorb Energy 3 (Fire &amp; Extreme Heat), Leap, Lurker In Darkness 3, Natural Weaponry 3 (Right Hand Of Doom), New Face 3, Regenerate 3, Terrify 2, Titan's Strength 5, Unholy Attribute (Strength 3, Stamina 5, Resolve 3)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/593374-should-i-allow-claimed-with-dread-powers-influences-numina-if-so-how?p=629898#post629898\"><b>Maximum Pseudo Essence/Per Turn:</b></a> 30/9</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What might the other Hellboy characters be in the NWOD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-17-2015, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}